1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,222
This is Kin.

2
00:00:04,222 --> 00:00:06,070
A savings circle on Solana.

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:11,333
Millions of people already save in circles called ajo, susu or tanda.

4
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:15,520
Everyone pays in each round, and one member takes the whole pot.

5
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:20,360
Today, the money lives in a notebook, and the trust lives in a group chat.

6
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,001
Kin puts the circle on chain.

7
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:24,934
Every member locks a small bond.

8
00:00:24,934 --> 00:00:27,652
Autopay is a capped allowance you can revoke.

9
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:31,940
And the payout order is drawn from on-chain data, so nobody can rig it.

10
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:36,602
You can watch a full circle play out without a wallet.

11
00:00:36,602 --> 00:00:39,131
Here, Diego misses a payment in round two.

12
00:00:39,131 --> 00:00:44,370
His bond covers it, the pot still pays out on time, and his Kin Score records the miss.

13
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,241
Connecting is one tap.

14
00:00:47,241 --> 00:00:49,432
Android asks which wallet to use.

15
00:00:49,432 --> 00:00:52,286
The wallet shows what Kin can and can't do.

16
00:00:52,286 --> 00:00:56,336
On devnet, Phantom adds a notice for apps it hasn't verified.

17
00:00:56,336 --> 00:00:57,797
Kin never holds a key.

18
00:00:57,797 --> 00:01:00,320
Every action is signed in your wallet.

19
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:04,699
Before you invite someone, paste their wallet.

20
00:01:04,699 --> 00:01:12,040
Kin reads their score straight from Solana, and shows their .skr or .sol name, so you see a name, not an address.

21
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:16,416
Your Kin Score follows your wallet into every circle.

22
00:01:16,416 --> 00:01:20,470
And on devnet, test funds come from a faucet program, in one tap.

23
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,909
Creating a circle takes a few fields.

24
00:01:24,909 --> 00:01:30,315
The token, the amount, how often rounds run, the number of members, and the bond.

25
00:01:30,315 --> 00:01:35,120
A circle can even require a Seeker Genesis Token before anyone can join.

26
00:01:36,010 --> 00:01:38,756
Turn on autopay, then join and lock your bond.

27
00:01:38,756 --> 00:01:45,500
The circle starts as soon as it fills, and anyone can collect a payment that is due, but never more than the cap.

28
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:49,231
You don't have to take our word for it.

29
00:01:49,231 --> 00:01:51,731
The Proof screen reads the chain directly.

30
00:01:51,731 --> 00:01:56,850
The vaults, the program, and every transaction, with no admin key that can move funds.

31
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,406
Kin is live on devnet.

32
00:01:59,406 --> 00:02:02,320
The code and the signed APK are on GitHub.

33
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,291
Save together.

34
00:02:03,291 --> 00:02:04,470
Get paid in turn.
